    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d375">

                <pb facs="0540" n="460" xml:id="pg460"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.C1199/234: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-09-25T14:00:00+01:00">September 25,
                            1936—2 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 25—9:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>444. Embassy’s 435, September 17, 4 p.m.<anchor n="17" xml:id="d375-f1"/> Foreign
                    Office handed me today following <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire:</hi>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“His Majesty’s Government fully agree with Mr. Cordell Hull as to the
                            satisfactory nature of the report of the Economic Committee of the
                            League of Nations and generally endorse its conclusions. They anticipate
                            that the question will be fully discussed at Geneva and they are not, of
                            course, aware what resolutions will be proposed or what concrete
                            suggestions will be put forward. They are not, therefore, at the moment,
                            in a position to state precisely what the final instructions to the
                            United Kingdom representatives will be, but their general attitude will
                            be as indicated above and His Majesty’s Government will be very pleased
                            to continue to keep in touch with Mr. Hull on the matter.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bingham</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
